{"title":"1983 AHSME Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Pdfresizer.com-pdf-convert.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/a/a6/Pdfresizer.com-pdf-convert.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"270\" height=\"255\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p><p>In the adjoining plane figure, sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/d/c9daba06f5ec9c5069f24bbeab9c7151ab4f68c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> are parallel, as are sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/2/c128243ea8125d0bb007b8132dcfa44461df73a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, \nand sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/2/bc2afec04e3636c80fa3d89e5468045595151c4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ED$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" />. Each side has length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Also, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/3/8b365654f655fd26910ab27a54a678c2d8415afd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle FAB = \\angle BCD = 60^\\circ$\" width=\"185\" height=\"13\" />. \nThe area of the figure is \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/0/4605bc57939c8614e629afd39980265341b12cd0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)} \\ \\frac{\\sqrt 3}{2} \\qquad  \\textbf{(B)} \\ 1 \\qquad  \\textbf{(C)} \\ \\frac{3}{2} \\qquad  \\textbf{(D)}\\ \\sqrt{3}\\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"387\" height=\"41\" />    \n</p><p><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/d/bddb9e658c2a3f38841b9348a1aa73ffaeadbc5e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] pair A, B, C, D, E, F; A = (0, 1.732); B = (0.5, 0.866); C = (0,0); D = (1, 0); E = (1.5, 0.866); F = (1, 1.732); draw(A--B--C--D--E--F--A); label(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, NW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, 3W); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, SW); label(&quot;$D$&quot;, D, SE); label(&quot;$E$&quot;, E, E); label(&quot;$F$&quot;, F, NE); draw(B--D, dashed+linewidth(0.5)); draw(B--E, dashed+linewidth(0.5)); draw(B--F, dashed+linewidth(0.5)); [/asy]\" width=\"232\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p>By rotating the diagram and drawing the dotted lines, we see that the figure can be divided into four equilateral triangles, each of side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The area of one such equilateral triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/1/90177bdc1942fbab4e77448f298e8766c268e049.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\cdot 1^2 = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"109\" height=\"41\" />, which gives a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/c/c0c397290160ed449644f1fceeb31435bddfc936.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}\\right) = \\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"117\" height=\"53\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/b/55bdade53f471aab49f63d1a734979cc0c636640.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{D}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"29\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME\" title=\"1983 AHSME\">1983 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1983 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1983 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1983\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_